# PART 5 — STAFF ASSIGNMENT SYSTEM

Enhance the existing assignment infrastructure.

One booking must support multiple assigned staff members.

An administrator must be able to:

- Select multiple staff members for one booking.
- Add staff members to an existing assignment.
- Remove or unassign staff members.
- Replace assigned staff.
- Assign or change the responsible supervisor.
- View assignment history.
- View each staff member's individual progress.

Preserve existing assignment functionality.

## Individual assignment progress

Each staff member must have an independent assignment status.

Recommended statuses:

- PENDING
- IN_PROGRESS
- SUBMITTED_FOR_REVIEW
- CHANGES_REQUESTED

A staff member must not be able to update another person's assignment.

When a staff member finishes their work, they must submit it for supervisor review.

Do not allow a staff member's submission to mark the overall booking completed.

## Staff completion submission

When submitting work for review, allow the staff member to provide:

- Completion notes.
- Description of the work performed.
- Optional supporting photos, if the existing storage architecture can safely support them.
- Any outstanding issues or concerns.

Validate all submitted information on the server.

Preserve the existing storage architecture and security rules.

