## Supervisor review process

When staff members submit their work, the supervisor should be able to:

1. Open the job.
2. Inspect staff completion reports.
3. Review individual staff contributions.
4. Add review notes.
5. Approve the work.
6. Request corrections when necessary.

A supervisor must not approve work that has not been submitted.

If corrections are requested:

- The affected staff member must be notified.
- Their assignment becomes CHANGES_REQUESTED.
- They can update their work and submit it again.
- The supervisor can review the new submission.
- Previous review history must remain available.

When the required work has been approved, the supervisor can mark the job as SUPERVISOR_APPROVED.

This must create an item in the administrator's final approval queue.

A supervisor must never be able to perform the administrator's final customer-facing booking completion action.

